<h1 local-id=3D"18068b4f5772" id=3D"ErrorHandling-1.PowerAutomate">1. Power=
Automate</h1>
<p local-id=3D"73f546112d99">In Power Automate, the <code>workflow()</code>=
 expression is a built-in function that returns <strong>metadata about the =
current flow run</strong>. This metadata is static and does not change duri=
ng the run of the flow.</p>
<p local-id=3D"0fd14ea666b5">Using the <code>workflow()</code> Function</p>
<p local-id=3D"9e853078279d">You can access this metadata by using the expr=
ession <code>workflow()</code> directly in any action that accepts expressi=
ons, such as a <strong>Compose</strong> action. This is particularly useful=
 for debugging, monitoring, or sending notifications with direct links to t=
he flow run details.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6eb81fcf61aa">Key Metadata Properties</p>
<p local-id=3D"b4e47182bd0a">The <code>workflow()</code> function returns a=
 JSON object with several key properties:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"30d67250-6c2a-4c5c-b0b0-9c21dbbd6b65">
<li local-id=3D"69aa50e1-8172-4f8b-812c-79f9ed7760d6">
<p local-id=3D"c88d02c49d83"><code>id</code>: The unique identifier (resour=
ce path) of the workflow.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"97fbc356-d7a0-42be-ad09-9824afd9748e">
<p local-id=3D"7ef75d2be812"><code>name</code>: The internal unique identif=
ier (GUID) of the workflow instance.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"39077096-2801-4c0a-bd3a-de39a5e023f5">
<p local-id=3D"818386c432ce"><code>type</code>: Specifies the resource type=
, typically <code>Microsoft.Logic/workflows</code>.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"3196aa7c-83d3-49ac-bfd0-ab78f2539fe8">
<p local-id=3D"dd99669b9ded"><code>location</code>: The Azure region where =
the workflow is deployed (e.g., <code>westeurope</code>).</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"2ebeaac4-5cae-42cb-b0a9-94e30fafb582">
<p local-id=3D"8c7fa5f46ed7"><code>tags</code>: An object containing additi=
onal tags, which can include the <code>environmentName</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"4b269b72ba35">Example Usage: Creating a Direct Link</p>
<p local-id=3D"68bc6ee2c774">The URL can be constructed using an expression=
 similar to this:
<br>
<code>"https://make.powerautomate.com/manage/environments/@{workflow().tags=
.environmentName}/flows/@{workflow().name}/runs/@{workflow()?['run']?['name=
']}"</code></p>
<p local-id=3D"bbe6feca0e3d"><strong>Error Log Table:</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"56d30a0342c7"><strong><span style=3D"color: rgb(191,38,0);">=
WRB Custom Error Log</span></strong></p>
